Add missing <cstdint> include for GCC 14+

GCC 14 tightened C++ header transitivity, so uintptr_t/uint32_t are no
longer implicitly available via other Qt/system headers. Documented in
this project's SETUP-RPI5.md as a known required patch when building
with HOSTCC=gcc-14; applies identically here since qt5declarative is
unmodified between boards.

--- a/src/qml/compiler/qv4compiler.cpp
+++ b/src/qml/compiler/qv4compiler.cpp
@@ -48,6 +48,8 @@
 #include <private/qqmlirbuilder_p.h>
 #include <QCryptographicHash>

+#include <cstdint>
+
 // Efficient implementation that takes advantage of powers of two.
 static inline size_t roundUpToMultipleOf(size_t divisor, size_t x)
 {
